      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-25T09:10:00Z",
      "note": "The attacker EOA sent exactly two transactions to its exploit contract; only the anchor touches the victim, so the anchor is both the earliest and the only defect-executing transaction. The victim is an unverified MEV bot contract, not a protocol, but the loss is a defect in deployed EVM code and is in cohort. It is not upgradeable: the runtime code hash is identical at the deployment block 18370467 and at block 18523343 and the EIP-1967 implementation slot is zero, so the exploited code is 21.4 days old, deployed by 0x1bda91e3a2e332428cf1a407821abecec0395427, which is unrelated to the attacker. Loss is the victim contract’s own net ERC-20 deltas in the exploit receipt. Because the implementation is unverified, the defect is characterised from the trace and BlockSec’s alert rather than from source; the code-age measurement does not depend on that characterisation."
    }
  ],
